### 2. Bot Initialization (Module Loading)

```
bot/run.py loads environment
    ↓
Validates safety systems
    ↓
Calls run_grid_strategy()
    ↓
bot/strategy/gridbot.py.__init__()
    ↓
Initialize modules in dependency order:
    1. GridCalculator (pure logic)
    2. PositionManager (owns lock)
    3. FillDetector (uses lock)
    4. DeltaClient (REST API)
    5. OrderManager (places orders)
    6. Reconciliation (syncs exchange)
    7. VolatilityHandler (safety)
    8. WebSocketManager (connection)
    9. WebSocketHandler (routing)
   10. Fill Handlers (LONG/SHORT)
   11. Monitoring Systems (5 layers)
    ↓
Wire callbacks:
    - WebSocket → price updates
    - WebSocket → fill detection
    - FillDetector → fill processing
    - OrderManager → aggressive polling
    ↓
Connect WebSocket
    ↓
Sync with exchange (adopt orphaned orders)
    ↓
Place initial grid order
    ↓
Start heartbeat loop (every 10-15 seconds)
```

### 3. Trading Cycle (LONG Mode Example)

```
1. Bot places BUY @ $109k (below market)
2. Price drops to $109k
3. Order fills
   ↓
   a. WebSocket v2/user_trades detects fill (0.05s)
   b. FillDetector deduplicates + queues
   c. Queue worker processes fill
   d. LongFillHandler called
      ↓
      - Updates PositionManager (add position)
      - Places TP @ $110k (entry + step)
      - Places next BUY @ $108k (entry - step)
      - Persists state to runtime_state.json
4. Price rises to $110k
5. TP order fills
   ↓
   a. WebSocket detects TP fill
   b. Remove position from tracking
   c. Profit: $1,000! ✅
6. Bot places new BUY @ $109k
7. Repeat infinitely...
```

