## 🚀 PM2 PROCESS MANAGEMENT

### Why PM2?

PM2 (Process Manager 2) replaced tmux for production deployment because:
- ✅ **Auto-restart on crash** - Bots automatically recover from failures
- ✅ **Resource monitoring** - Built-in CPU/memory tracking
- ✅ **Log management** - Automatic log rotation and aggregation
- ✅ **Zero-downtime reload** - Update code without stopping trading
- ✅ **Startup on boot** - Bots auto-start after macOS restarts
- ✅ **WebUI integration** - Control bots from web dashboard

### PM2 Processes (ecosystem.config.js)

| Process Name | Script | Auto-Restart | Memory Limit | Purpose |
|-------------|--------|--------------|--------------|---------|
| `gridbot-live` | bot/run.py | ✅ Yes | 500MB | Live trading bot |
| `gridbot-demo` | bot/run.py | ✅ Yes | 500MB | Demo trading bot |
| `guardian-live` | bot/guardian/guardian_bot.py | ✅ Yes | 300MB | Live loss protection |
| `guardian-demo` | bot/guardian/guardian_bot.py | ✅ Yes | 300MB | Demo loss protection |
| `heartbeat-monitor` | bot/heartbeat/monitor.py | ✅ Yes | 200MB | Dead man's switch |
| `webui-backend` | webui/backend/app.py | ✅ Yes | 500MB | Web interface |

### PM2 Quick Reference

```bash
# Status & Monitoring
pm2 list                    # Show all processes
pm2 status                  # Same as list
pm2 monit                   # Real-time monitoring (CPU/memory/logs)
pm2 describe gridbot-live   # Detailed process info

# Starting
pm2 start ecosystem.config.js                # Start all
pm2 start ecosystem.config.js --only gridbot-live  # Start specific
./pm2_gridbot.sh start live                  # Using helper script

# Stopping (Graceful - 30s timeout)
pm2 stop gridbot-live       # Stop single process
pm2 stop all                # Stop all processes
./pm2_gridbot.sh stop live  # Using helper script

# Restarting
pm2 restart gridbot-live    # Hard restart (stops then starts)
pm2 reload gridbot-live     # Zero-downtime reload (if supported)
./pm2_gridbot.sh restart live

# Logs
pm2 logs                    # All logs (live stream)
pm2 logs gridbot-live       # Single process logs
pm2 logs gridbot-live --lines 200  # Last 200 lines
pm2 flush                   # Clear all logs
./pm2_gridbot.sh logs live  # Using helper script

# Maintenance
pm2 save                    # Save current process list
pm2 resurrect               # Restore saved processes
pm2 startup                 # Enable auto-start on boot (run once)
pm2 unstartup               # Disable auto-start
pm2 update                  # Update PM2 daemon

# Advanced
pm2 reset gridbot-live      # Reset restart counter
pm2 delete gridbot-live     # Remove from PM2 (stops first)
pm2 kill                    # Kill PM2 daemon (stops all)
```

### Auto-Start on Boot

PM2 is configured to start all bots automatically when macOS boots:

```bash
# Setup (already done, run once)
pm2 startup
pm2 save

# This creates LaunchAgent: ~/Library/LaunchAgents/pm2.<user>.plist
# PM2 daemon starts at login → resurrects saved processes
```

